Spec: Feature OIDC UserInfo Profile Sync

Purpose:
  After a successful OIDC login, retrieve the claims of the identity provider's UserInfo endpoint on the server and use them, together with the ID token claims, to keep first name, last name, e-mail and department of `admin_users` up to date. The IdP access token never leaves the server.

Platform: Rust/Axum/PostgreSQL

References:
  ../../../mitm-2.sdd
  ../../../core-layer/core-layer.sdd
  ../../../core-layer/mitm_http-server/specs/api_spec.sdd
  ../oidc-authentication/oidc-authentication.sdd
  ../oidc-profile-sync/oidc-profile-sync.sdd
  ../me-profile-email/me-profile-email.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /core-layer/mitm_http-server/**
  /CHANGELOG.md

Must:
  After the ID token is validated and the user is known and active, mitm_http-server requests the IdP UserInfo endpoint (from the discovery document) with the access token of the token response and the ID token `sub` as expected subject; a UserInfo response for another subject is rejected.
  A filled UserInfo claim takes precedence over the ID token claim: `given_name` → `first_name`, `family_name` → `last_name`, `email` → `email`; the claim named by `OIDC_DEPARTMENT_CLAIM` (default `department`, string value) → `department`.
  A claim that is missing or empty after trimming in both sources leaves the stored value unchanged.
  If the IdP has no UserInfo endpoint, or the request fails or times out, the login continues with the ID token claims; a failed request is logged with level `WARN` to system_logs.
  OIDC requests to the IdP (discovery, token, UserInfo) time out after 10 seconds.

Must not:
  Send the IdP access token, ID token or UserInfo response to the browser or store them.
  Request UserInfo for a rejected login (unknown or inactive user, invalid token).
  Change the API contract; `GET /api/v1/auth/me` already returns `first_name`, `last_name`, `department` and `email`.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 UserInfo request with expected subject and custom claim type for the department claim.
  [x] #2 Merge UserInfo and ID token claims; sync `department` in addition to name and e-mail.
  [x] #3 `OIDC_DEPARTMENT_CLAIM`, request timeout, failure handling.
  [x] #4 Unit tests, README, API documentation, CHANGELOG.

Done when:
  `cargo build` and `cargo test` of mitm-http-server succeed, and an OIDC login stores the UserInfo `department` in `admin_users.department`.

Scenario: department from UserInfo
  Given the active user `Q225265` signs in via OIDC
  And the ID token has no `department` claim
  And the UserInfo response has `department` `FG-123`
  When the callback completes
  Then `admin_users.department` of `Q225265` is `FG-123`

Scenario: UserInfo overrides ID token
  Given the ID token has `email` `old@example.com`
  And the UserInfo response has `email` `new@example.com`
  When the callback completes
  Then `admin_users.email` is `new@example.com`

Scenario: UserInfo unavailable
  Given the UserInfo request fails
  When the callback completes
  Then the user is signed in with the ID token claims
  And system_logs contains a `WARN` entry for the failed UserInfo request
